    "publishedAt": "2026-11-10",
    "summary": "Royal Australasian College of Surgeons (RACS) targets saving AU$2.1 million over five years and up to 21,000 kWh annually Project migration finishes ahead of licensing renewal with no interruption to RACS's members Melbourne, Australia, November 10, 2026 – HPE (NYSE: HPE) today announced that the Royal Australasian College of Surgeons (RACS) has moved its remaining on-premises workloads to HPE Private Cloud . Across its on-premises environment and disaster recovery site, the college expects to save about AU$2.1 million over five years as its technology roadmap progresses. By modernizing its aging infrastructure, RACS improved performance and reduced its hardware footprint, core count, and licensing costs. By reducing the cost and effort of running core systems while retaining room to grow, RACS creates more capacity to invest in the digital experiences that support surgeons throughout their careers.",
