    "sourceUrl": "https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/semiconductors/tsmcs-a14-1-4nm-class-node-is-ready-for-chip-design-boost-cells-promise-14-percent-performance-uplift-or-23-percent-power-cut-over-n2p",
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-26",
    "summary": "TSMC announces availability of its version 0.9 process design kit for its A14 manufacturing technology. Availability of the v0.9 version of PDK signals that the fabrication process is generally ready for design and production. A14 uses TSMC's 2 nd Generation nanosheet transistors and its NanoFlex Pro standard cell architecture, which supports Boost Cells to enable higher performance as well as Low-Power Cells to reduce power consumption. This table summarizes A14 v0.9 certification for our three major EDA partners, Cadence, Synopsys, and Siemens, across automatic placement and routing, library characterization, timing, power, EM/IR, and other sign-off flows.",
    "whyItMatters": "先进封装和制程节奏会决定 AI 芯片交付能力，间接影响服务器整机和机柜组件订单能见度。",
