    "summary": "Building on the technology and architecture of the KIOXIA GP1 Series SSD announced in August 2026, the KIOXIA GP2 Series delivers over 18 million random read IOPS at a 512-byte block size, nearly double the performance of its predecessor. It is also expected to deliver sequential read throughput of up to 28 GB/s, enough to saturate a PCIe 6.0 x4 link. Super High IOPS SSDs can expand the effective capacity of a GPU system's High Bandwidth Memory (HBM) by providing an additional flash-based memory tier directly accessible by the GPU, supporting industry efforts to improve AI system capability and efficiency.",
