    "summary": "Threats tied to a up to 1GW project in Lackawanna County Police in Pennsylvania have made arrests and are undertaking an investigation concerning ongoing threats made to the local council after it approved a controversial data center development in the town of Olyphant. At full build-out, the site could consume up to 1GW of electricity. As part of the approval, the council had agreed to a community benefits agreement with the developer to secure $101 million over the next 15 years to support funding for services and offset residential taxes. ERCOR has sought to mitigate community concerns by stating that it intends to deploy closed-loop cooling systems and enclose backup generators within the buildings to dampen sound.",
