    "publishedAt": "2026-11-26",
    "summary": "The facility will have an initial capacity of 1MW, scalable up to 6MW Latin American operator Tecto Data Centers announced TREC1, its first data center in Recife, Pernambuco state, Brazil. The company did not disclose the investment amount or details about the facility’s exact location, but said the new data center represents another step in its strategy dubbed “AI Grid,” which distributes processing capacity across different regions to bring infrastructure closer to the locations where data is generated and consumed. Earlier this year, the company announced a $2 billion investment plan (approximately 11.7 billion reais) between 2026 and 2028, including the construction of five new data centers later this year and its entry into the enterprise market. In Fortaleza, Tecto operates Big Lobster, which opened in 2023, and Mega Lobster, a 20MW data center that opened in October 2025 in Praia do Futuro, with an investment of over 550 million reais.",
